BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the layered architecture of the OSI 7-Layer Reference Model. Detail the functions, services, and representative protocol standards associated with each of the seven layers.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architectural Principle:) Tj
T*
(   Developed by ISO in 1984, the Open Systems Interconnection \(OSI\) reference model establishes an) Tj
T*
(   open framework for computer network communications.) Tj
T*
(   Layering enforces abstraction, modularity, and encapsulation: each layer provides distinct) Tj
T*
(   services to the layer above while shielding it from implementation details.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Detailed Breakdown of the Seven Layers:) Tj
T*
(   - Layer 1: Physical Layer:) Tj
T*
(   * Functions: Transmission and reception of raw, unstructured bit streams over physical) Tj
T*
(   transmission media.) Tj
T*
(   * Defines: Voltage levels, bit timing, signal modulation, physical connectors \(RJ-45, LC/SC) Tj
T*
(   fiber\), pinouts, transmission modes \(simplex, duplex\).) Tj
T*
(   * Standards: IEEE 802.3 physical layer, RS-232, V.35, DSL, SONET/SDH, OTN.) Tj
T*
(   - Layer 2: Data Link Layer:) Tj
T*
(   * Functions: Transforms error-prone physical links into reliable links; framing, physical MAC) Tj
T*
(   addressing, flow control, error detection \(CRC\).) Tj
T*
(   * Sublayers: Logical Link Control \(LLC - IEEE 802.2\) and Media Access Control \(MAC - IEEE 802.3) Tj
T*
(   Ethernet, 802.11 Wi-Fi\).) Tj
T*
(   * Hardware: Network Interface Cards \(NICs\), Layer 2 Bridges and Switches.) Tj
T*
(   - Layer 3: Network Layer:) Tj
T*
(   * Functions: Host-to-host packet delivery across heterogeneous internetworks, logical) Tj
T*
(   addressing \(IPv4/IPv6\), routing, packet fragmentation/reassembly.) Tj
T*
(   * Protocols: IPv4, IPv6, ICMP, ARP, OSPF, BGP, RIP. Hardware: Routers, Layer 3 Switches.) Tj
T*
(   - Layer 4: Transport Layer:) Tj
T*
(   * Functions: True end-to-end, process-to-process delivery; service-point \(port\) addressing,) Tj
T*
(   segmentation/reassembly, connection management,) Tj
T*
(   flow control \(sliding window\), and error recovery \(ACKs, retransmissions\).) Tj
T*
(   * Protocols: TCP \(connection-oriented, reliable\), UDP \(connectionless, fast\).) Tj
T*
(   - Layer 5: Session Layer:) Tj
T*
(   * Functions: Establishes, maintains, synchronizes, and terminates dialogues between distributed) Tj
T*
(   software processes; manages token control and synchronization checkpoints.) Tj
T*
(   * Protocols: RPC, NetBIOS, PPTP, SIP.) Tj
T*
(   - Layer 6: Presentation Layer:) Tj
T*
(   * Functions: Syntactic and semantic translation of data between communicating systems; data) Tj
T*
(   formatting \(ASCII, EBCDIC, Unicode\), data compression \(JPEG, MPEG, gzip\), and) Tj
T*
(   encryption/decryption \(TLS/SSL\).) Tj
T*
(   - Layer 7: Application Layer:) Tj
T*
(   * Functions: Directly provides network services to user applications; network virtual terminal,) Tj
T*
(   file transfer, electronic mail, directory lookups.) Tj
T*
(   * Protocols: HTTP/HTTPS, DNS, SMTP, POP3, IMAP, FTP, SSH, Telnet, SNMP.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
