(   comprehensive theoretical model BEFORE protocols were implemented.) Tj
T*
(   Strictly distinguishes between Services, Interfaces, and Protocols. Clean 7-layer theoretical) Tj
T*
(   separation.) Tj
T*
(   - TCP/IP Suite: Developed bottom-up by DARPA/ARPA researchers with a pragmatic 'rough consensus) Tj
T*
(   and running code' philosophy.) Tj
T*
(   Designed specifically for military survivability and internetworking across disparate networks;) Tj
T*
(   protocols were created first, and the model was documented later.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Layer-by-Layer Mapping:) Tj
T*
(   - OSI Layers 7, 6, 5 \(Application, Presentation, Session\) -> Mapped into a single unified) Tj
T*
(   TCP/IP Application Layer.) Tj
T*
(   - OSI Layer 4 \(Transport\) -> Corresponds directly to TCP/IP Transport Layer \(Host-to-Host) Tj
T*
(   Layer: TCP, UDP\).) Tj
T*
(   - OSI Layer 3 \(Network\) -> Corresponds directly to TCP/IP Internet Layer \(IP, ICMP, ARP\).) Tj
T*
(   - OSI Layers 2, 1 \(Data Link, Physical\) -> Mapped into TCP/IP Network Access Layer \(or Link) Tj
T*
(   Layer / Host-to-Network Layer\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Decisive Reasons for TCP/IP's Global Victory:) Tj
T*
(   - 1. Pragmatic Implementation & Timing: TCP/IP code was bundled freely with BSD UNIX \(4.2BSD in) Tj
T*
(   1983\), providing universities and vendors with an instant, robust, working protocol stack.) Tj
T*
(   - 2. Bureaucratic Overhead of OSI: OSI standard specifications were enormous, overly complex,) Tj
T*
(   and bogged down in committee debates for years.) Tj
T*
(   - 3. Redundancy in OSI: OSI implemented flow control and error control redundantly across) Tj
T*
(   multiple layers \(Layer 2, Layer 3, and Layer 4\), increasing software overhead.) Tj
T*
(   - 4. End-to-End Design Principle: TCP/IP keeps the network core simple and stateless \(smart) Tj
T*
(   endpoints, dumb network\), scaling gracefully to billions of nodes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
