BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate and compare the physical characteristics, transmission mechanisms, bandwidth capabilities, and structural shielding of Guided Transmission Media: Twisted Pair, Coaxial Cable, and Fiber Optic Cable.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Twisted-Pair Copper Cable \(UTP / STP\):) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Construction: Insulated copper conductors \(typically 22 to 24 AWG\) twisted into) Tj
T*
(   pairs. Twisting cancels differential electromagnetic crosstalk.) Tj
T*
(   - Shielding: UTP lacks metallic shielding; STP incorporates overall foil/braid shields \(F/UTP,) Tj
T*
(   S/FTP\) to eliminate alien crosstalk in industrial environments.) Tj
T*
(   - Performance: Bandwidth spans from 100 MHz \(Cat 5e, 1 Gbps up to 100 m\) to 500 MHz \(Cat 6a, 10) Tj
T*
(   Gbps up to 100 m\) and 2000 MHz \(Cat 8, 40 Gbps up to 30 m\).) Tj
T*
(   - Limitations: High high-frequency attenuation, susceptibility to external EMI, distance) Tj
T*
(   strictly capped at 100 meters per channel.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Coaxial Cable:) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Construction: Solid or stranded central copper core surrounded by cylindrical) Tj
T*
(   dielectric insulator, concentric braided metal shielding, and protective outer PVC jacket.) Tj
T*
(   - Shielding: Concentric geometry provides excellent electromagnetic shielding and consistent) Tj
T*
(   characteristic impedance \(50 Ohm for RF, 75 Ohm for CATV/video\).) Tj
T*
(   - Performance: Supports frequencies up to 1 GHz over several hundred meters with lower) Tj
T*
(   attenuation than twisted pair.) Tj
T*
(   - Limitations: Bulky, stiffer, higher termination cost; largely displaced by UTP in LANs,) Tj
T*
(   though dominant in DOCSIS hybrid fiber-coax \(HFC\) broadband.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Fiber-Optic Cable \(Single-Mode & Multi-Mode\):) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Construction: Ultra-pure silica glass core surrounded by glass cladding with) Tj
T*
