/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Pulse Code Modulation \(PCM\). Detail the three sequential stages: Sampling, Quantization, and Encoding. Explain the Nyquist sampling criterion and calculate the standard transmission bitrate for a telephone PCM voice channel.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Overview of Pulse Code Modulation \(PCM\):) Tj
T*
(   Invented by Alec Reeves in 1937, PCM is the foundational digital conversion standard used) Tj
T*
(   globally to convert continuous analog signals into digital bit streams.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Three Sequential Operations:) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 1: Periodic Sampling \(PAM - Pulse Amplitude Modulation\):) Tj
T*
(   * The continuous analog signal x\(t\) is sampled at discrete, uniformly spaced time intervals T_s) Tj
T*
