(   = 1 / f_s.) Tj
T*
(   * Nyquist Criterion: To prevent aliasing \(spectral overlap\), the sampling rate f_s must be at) Tj
T*
(   least twice the highest frequency component B present in the signal: f_s >= 2 * B.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 2: Quantization:) Tj
T*
(   * The infinite continuous voltage amplitudes of the PAM samples are mapped onto a finite set of) Tj
T*
(   L discrete, predetermined quantization levels.) Tj
T*
(   * If step size is Delta, the maximum quantization error is e_max = Delta / 2.) Tj
T*
(   * In voice communications, non-uniform logarithmic companding \(mu-law in North America, A-law) Tj
T*
(   in Europe\) provides finer quantization steps for quiet sounds and coarser steps for loud) Tj
T*
(   sounds, maintaining constant SNR.) Tj
T*
(   - Stage 3: Binary Encoding:) Tj
T*
(   * Each quantized amplitude level is converted into an n-bit binary code word, where L = 2^n =>) Tj
T*
(   n = log2\(L\) bits per sample.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Standard Digital Telephone Voice Channel Calculation \(DS0 Channel\):) Tj
T*
(   - Analog human voice bandwidth is bandlimited by low-pass anti-aliasing filters to B = 4 kHz) Tj
T*
(   \(300 Hz to 3400 Hz standard speech band\).) Tj
T*
(   - Nyquist Sampling Rate: f_s = 2 * B = 2 * 4,000 = 8,000 samples per second.) Tj
T*
(   - Quantization Resolution: n = 8 bits per sample \(L = 256 discrete quantization levels\).) Tj
T*
(   - Digital Bitrate: Bitrate = f_s * n = 8,000 samples/s * 8 bits/sample = 64,000 bps = 64 kbps.) Tj
T*
(   - This fundamental 64 kbps stream defines the standard International Digital Signal Level 0) Tj
T*
(   \(DS0\) voice channel.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
